1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:02,270
Your dog isn't being dramatic about thunder.

2
00:00:02,540 --> 00:00:05,400
About one in three dogs is afraid of loud noises,

3
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,770
and storms hit them with more than noise.

4
00:00:08,210 --> 00:00:10,890
Some dogs start pacing before you hear a thing.

5
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:12,690
They may feel the air pressure drop.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,420
One theory: storms also charge the air,

7
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:18,750
so static builds up in their fur and gives them tiny shocks.

8
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:21,940
That might be why some dogs hide in the bathtub,

9
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:23,270
right next to the pipes.

10
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:25,990
And comforting them won't make the fear worse.

11
00:00:26,390 --> 00:00:27,710
Vets call that a myth.

12
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:31,060
So when the sky rumbles and they squeeze in next to you,

13
00:00:31,060 --> 00:00:32,200
hold them close, because
